{
  "summary": "This study investigates covalent integration of maleimide-functionalized conjugated polymers with Shewanella oneidensis to enhance microbial electrosynthesis. The approach utilized in situ click reactions with cytochrome thiols to create stable bio-interfaces. Results showed doubled bacterial adhesion, 23-fold increased electron transfer, and 6-fold higher electrochemical reduction compared to unmodified bacteria. The covalent strategy significantly improved charge output and succinate yield while upregulating respiratory proteins.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Covalent maleimide-functionalized conjugated polymers doubled bacterial adhesion via in situ click reactions with cytochrome thiols",
    "23-fold increase in electron transfer and 6-fold improvement in electrochemical reduction relative to bare S. oneidensis",
    "2-fold enhancement in total charge output and succinate yield with upregulation of respiratory protein complexes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This covalent biotic-abiotic interface engineering strategy establishes a molecular-level approach for optimizing microbial electrosynthesis, advancing sustainable carbon conversion through enhanced electron transfer mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines immune mechanisms underlying oral tolerance in preventing IgE-mediated food allergy. It synthesizes how early dietary antigen exposure establishes durable tolerance through coordinated cellular pathways: transcellular antigen transport via goblet cell-associated passages, tolerogenic antigen presentation by RORγt+ APCs and cDCs, regulatory T cell induction, and germinal center regulation of antibody responses. Genetic and environmental factors modulate these pathways, while infections can disrupt tolerance. The study highlights tolerance and allergy as competing immune states stabilized by redundant regulatory circuits.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Early dietary antigen exposure during infancy prevents IgE-mediated food allergy through oral tolerance mechanisms",
    "Oral tolerance requires coordinated activity of transcellular antigen transport, tolerogenic APCs, regulatory T cells, and germinal center regulation",
    "Infections can disrupt established oral tolerance by reprogramming tolerogenic antigen-presenting cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review provides a comprehensive model of multilayered immune mechanisms that govern oral tolerance, clarifying how dietary antigen exposure can prevent food allergy while highlighting the critical role of redundant regulatory circuits in maintaining immune homeostasis."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether transient dietary changes during acute inflammation influence long-term immune memory. Using lean mice with type 17 skin inflammation, researchers found that a 4-day high-fat diet (HFD) exposure at disease onset exacerbates inflammation to levels seen in chronic obesity. The effect is confined to a specific 4-day window; HFD outside this window has no impact. Switching obese mice to a low-fat diet during the same window reduces disease severity. Mechanistically, HFD rapidly recruits neutrophils, which express Nlrp3 and Il1b, driving pathogenic TH17 cell activation. After recovery, a chromatin-poised tissue-resident memory T cell population persists, causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence despite subsequent LFD. The findings demonstrate that dietary state during a narrow temporal window can durably reprogram disease trajectory through neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β signaling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Transient high-fat diet exposure at disease onset exacerbates acute type 17 skin inflammation in lean mice to chronic obesity levels",
    "The inflammatory effect is restricted to a 4-day peri-initiation window; HFD outside this window has no impact",
    "Neutrophil recruitment and NLRP3-IL-1β signaling drive pathogenic TH17 cell activation, with persistent tissue-resident memory T cells causing exaggerated inflammation upon recurrence"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a critical temporal window where transient dietary changes can durably reprogram immune memory via neutrophil-NLRP3-IL-1β signaling, revealing how short-lived physiological states may become embedded in tissue inflammation responses."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates precise growth of ultrathin amorphous indium oxide (In2O3) using layered precursor-guided synthesis. By oxidizing a layered InSe precursor within BEOL-compatible thermal conditions, the researchers achieved atomically smooth In2O3 films as thin as 0.63 nm. The material exhibited nondegenerate electronic properties with low carrier density (2.8 × 1018 cm-3), minimal interface traps, and high electrostatic uniformity. These findings enable sub-3 nm channel transistors with near-zero threshold voltage and low hysteresis, advancing ultrathin oxide semiconductor applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Atomically smooth In2O3 films as thin as 0.63 nm achieved via layered precursor oxidation",
    "Nondegenerate electronic properties with carrier density of 2.8 × 1018 cm-3 and low interface trap density",
    "Sub-3 nm channel transistors showing near-zero threshold voltage and negligible hysteresis (<10 mV)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a scalable method for ultrathin amorphous oxide semiconductors with enhanced electronic properties, enabling next-generation nanoelectronic devices with improved stability and performance."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines antigen-specific immunotherapy (ASI) for type 1 diabetes (T1D), addressing the autoimmune destruction of pancreatic β-cells. It evaluates ASI mechanisms like clonal deletion, immune deviation, regulatory T cell induction, and tolerogenic antigen presentation. The study highlights ASI's potential to preserve β-cell function and modify disease progression, emphasizing recent advances in autoantigen targeting and clinical translation strategies.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ASI mechanisms include clonal deletion, immune deviation, and regulatory T cell induction",
    "ASI may preserve residual β-cell function and alter disease progression",
    "Recent advances focus on autoantigen targeting and clinical translation strategies"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review advances understanding of how antigen-specific immunotherapy can potentially restore immune tolerance in type 1 diabetes by targeting autoimmune mechanisms."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how human replication forks restart after stalling, focusing on the role of the replisome. Using purified human proteins, the authors reconstituted fork stalling and restart to demonstrate that the CMG helicase directs the primase-polymerase PRIMPOL for efficient leading-strand priming during fork restart. The interaction between PRIMPOL and replication protein A was found non-essential, while direct CMG-PRIMPOL binding ensures minimal post-replicative gaps. Ablating this interaction abolished fork restart in vitro and DNA damage tolerance in cells.",
  "key_findings": [
    "CMG helicase directs PRIMPOL for efficient replication fork restart",
    "Direct CMG-PRIMPOL binding targets PRIMPOL specifically for leading-strand priming",
    "Ablating CMG-PRIMPOL interaction abolishes fork restart in vitro and PRIMPOL-dependent DNA damage tolerance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PRIMPOL as an integrated replisome component dedicated to leading-strand priming, providing mechanistic insight into how replication forks are restarted after stalling to maintain genomic stability."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates thermomechanical stress regulation in perovskite solar cells (PSCs) using a dynamic molecular scaffold. The researchers developed a crosslinked polydisulfide scaffold via in situ polymerization of DL-α-lipoic acid-N-hydroxysuccinimide ester (LA-NHS) at grain boundaries. The scaffold buffers thermal stress, anchors the perovskite lattice, and passivates defects through reversible disulfide exchange. Optimized PSCs achieved 27.19% power conversion efficiency with 91.71% retention after 150 thermal cycles (15–100°C) and 85.72% after 1500 hours at 85°C, demonstrating enhanced thermal stability and scalability.",
  "key_findings": [
    "In situ polymerization of LA-NHS establishes a crosslinked polydisulfide scaffold at grain boundaries",
    "The scaffold buffers thermal stress, anchors the perovskite lattice, and passivates defects via reversible disulfide exchange",
    "PSCs retained 91.71% efficiency after 150 thermal cycles (15–100°C) and 85.72% after 1500 hours at 85°C"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides a dynamic molecular scaffold strategy for managing thermomechanical degradation in perovskite solar cells, enabling enhanced thermal stability and scalable high-efficiency photovoltaics through stress buffering, lattice anchoring, and adaptive defect healing."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how Huanglian Jiedu Decoction modulates T lymphocyte-microglia interactions in ischemic stroke. Using rat models of cerebral ischemia-reperfusion injury, Jurkat T cell inflammation assays, and Transwell co-cultures, the research demonstrated that the decoction promotes Treg conversion in the brain, enhances M2 microglial polarization via IL-10/JAK1/STAT3 signaling, and reduces neuroinflammation. These mechanisms suggest a novel immunomodulatory pathway for stroke treatment.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Huanglian Jiedu Decoction promotes conversion of CD4+ T cells into regulatory T cells in brain tissue",
    "The decoction induces M2 microglial polarization through IL-10/JAK1/STAT3 signaling",
    "It alleviates cerebral ischemia-reperfusion injury and suppresses central inflammatory responses"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a specific immunomodulatory mechanism by which a traditional Chinese medicine decoction regulates T lymphocyte-microglia crosstalk to mitigate neuroinflammation in ischemic stroke."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates compact optical systems for all-day augmented reality glasses using metasurface waveguides. Researchers developed a dual-layer metasurface-based waveguide (meta-WG) that achieves a 30° field of view, an 8×8 mm² eyebox, and 1,938 nits luminance efficiency within a 1.5-mm-thick form factor. The prototype demonstrates stable outdoor performance, addressing trade-offs in optical efficiency, field of view, and eyebox size for practical AR applications.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dual-layer metasurface waveguide achieves 30° field of view",
    "Maintains 8×8 mm² eyebox and 1,938 nits luminance efficiency",
    "Operates stably under outdoor ambient illumination"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach expands light control degrees of freedom beyond conventional diffractive waveguides, enabling scalable trade-offs between optical efficiency, field of view, and form factor for practical augmented reality displays."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how air-stable radical additives influence spin-dependent recombination in high-efficiency organic solar cells. Using electron paramagnetic resonance and spectroscopic techniques, researchers confirmed the radical character of TTM-1Cz and its structural impact on crystalline coherence. The additive reduced triplet-associated recombination signals, leading to a 20.63% power conversion efficiency in optimized devices. The findings demonstrate that radical additives can modulate spin-dependent recombination through both structural and spin-active mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "TTM-1Cz retains radical character post-solution processing",
    "Radical additive reduces late-time triplet-associated recombination signals",
    "Optimized device achieves 20.63% power conversion efficiency"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a design strategy for radical additives that simultaneously enhance crystalline order and suppress spin-dependent recombination in organic solar cells, offering a dual mechanism for improving device efficiency."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated a gut-brain co-therapy approach for inflammatory bowel disease (IBD)-associated anxiety and depression using a probiotic-based sequential delivery system. The researchers engineered a microecological preparation combining Clostridium butyricum loaded with 5-aminosalicylic acid (5-ASA) and indole-3-acetic acid (IAA) within a pH-responsive polymer layer. The system delivered 5-ASA to the colon and IAA to the brain, improving intestinal barrier function, macrophage polarization, Th17/Treg balance, and reducing anxiety/depression-like behaviors in colitis mice while preventing disease recurrence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The delivery system simultaneously targeted intestinal inflammation and neuroinflammation via sequential release of 5-ASA and IAA",
    "It restored intestinal homeostasis by promoting macrophage M2 polarization and Th17/Treg balance",
    "The system alleviated anxiety/depression-like behaviors and prevented inflammatory recurrence in colitis models"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a novel gut-brain co-therapy strategy that effectively addresses both intestinal and psychiatric comorbidities in IBD through coordinated neuroimmune modulation and local tissue repair."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the timing and processes of early Earth crust formation by analyzing 3.95-Gyr-old North China Craton rocks. Using geochemical and isotopic data from trondhjemitic gneiss, the research identifies elevated δ18O and positive εHf(t) values, indicating a Hadean mantle depleted source. The findings suggest rapid subduction of oceanic crust at high pressure, providing evidence for early plate tectonics starting by 3.95 Gyr ago.",
  "key_findings": [
    "3.95-Gyr-old trondhjemitic gneiss from North China Craton",
    "Elevated δ18O values (+6.77 ± 0.23‰) and positive εHf(t) values (+1.45 ± 0.27)",
    "High-pressure origin via rapid subduction of oceanic crust"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides direct evidence of Hadean mantle depletion and early subduction processes, advancing understanding of Earth's crustal evolution and the onset of plate tectonics by 3.95 billion years ago."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates waveguided liquid crystal elastomer fiber actuators with integrated self-sensing capabilities for confined environments. The researchers designed a sheath-core optical fiber using a liquid crystal elastomer core and a conductive carbon nanotube/carbon black sheath. Near-infrared light activation enabled reversible contractions up to 38% and a load capacity 320 times the actuator's weight. The conductive sheath provided real-time strain monitoring via resistance changes, allowing programmable gripping in tight spaces without external sensors.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Reversible contractions of up to 38% via near-infrared light activation",
    "Load-bearing capacity exceeding 320 times the actuator's weight",
    "Conductive sheath enables real-time strain monitoring through resistance changes"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a multifunctional soft actuator platform that integrates photothermal actuation and self-sensing within a single fiber architecture for confined environments, advancing capabilities for soft robotics in spatially restricted settings."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated cross-species single-cell, single-nucleus, and spatial transcriptomics data to characterize prostate remodeling in aging and benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH). By analyzing Homo sapiens, Mus musculus, and Macaca fascicularis samples, it identified species-specific immune cell enrichments (e.g., CD4_Tem, CD4_Treg, CD8_CTL) and tissue features linked to inflammation, angiogenesis, and extracellular matrix remodeling in older age groups. The findings reveal conserved remodeling patterns across species associated with prostate aging and BPH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Increased abundance of CD4_Tem, CD4_Treg, CD8_CTL, Macro_IL1B, and Macro_LYVE1 in middle-aged or old groups",
    "Basal, club, and hillock cells showed higher EMT-related and ECM remodeling features in old groups",
    "Fibro_IL1R1, Fibro_C7, and SMC_CNN1 were enriched in old groups with active inflammation and ECM remodeling pathways"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides cross-species insights into conserved immune and tissue remodeling mechanisms underlying prostate aging and BPH, advancing understanding of age-related pathophysiology across species."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how crystal integrity in potassium poly(heptazine imide) (PHI-K) enhances photoreforming selectivity for polyesters. Using molten-salt recrystallization, the researchers produced nanocrystals with reduced cyano content and improved lattice coherence. Spectroscopic and theoretical analyses revealed that suppressing bulk hole traps increased exciton decay times from 69.52 to 984.72 ps. Under AM 1.5G irradiation, crystalline PHI-K achieved high carbon yields (95.2% for polyglycolic acid, 92.5% for poly(lactic acid)) and significant hydrogen evolution rates (42.6 and 26.0 mmol g-1 h-1).",
  "key_findings": [
    "PHI-K nanocrystals with enhanced lattice coherence suppress bulk hole traps",
    "Extended exciton-associated absorption decay time from 69.52 to 984.72 ps",
    "High carbon yields (95.2% and 92.5%) and hydrogen evolution rates (42.6 and 26.0 mmol g-1 h-1) for polyesters under AM 1.5G irradiation"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes crystal integrity as a critical principle for organic semiconductors to maintain bulk charge retention and enable selective bond conversion in photocatalytic reactions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study evaluated combining venetoclax (a BCL-2 inhibitor) with abatacept (CD28 costimulation blockade) to prevent graft-versus-host disease (GVHD) post-haploidentical hematopoietic cell transplantation. In murine models, the VEN+ABA regimen matched cyclophosphamide-based prophylaxis in GVHD prevention while maintaining graft-versus-leukemia effects and showing enhanced regulatory T cell ratios. The combination induced apoptosis specifically in alloreactive T cells without compromising antitumor activity.",
  "key_findings": [
    "VEN+ABA prevented GVHD comparably to cyclophusingamide monotherapy and superior to cyclophosphamide-based regimens",
    "VEN+ABA maintained graft-versus-leukemia effects while improving regulatory T cell ratios",
    "The combination selectively induced apoptosis in alloreactive T cells without affecting graft-versus-leukemia activity"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This approach provides a targeted strategy for GVHD prophylaxis by preferentially eliminating alloreactive T cells through BCL-2 inhibition and costimulation blockade, potentially reducing toxicity associated with alkylating agents."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines engineering strategies to overcome CIGS bottom cell limitations in perovskite/CIGS tandem solar cells. It identifies Ga-gradient bandgap engineering, alkali post-deposition treatments, Ag alloying for low-.temperature growth, and interface optimization as key approaches. The study demonstrates how surface morphology and defect chemistry impact carrier recombination and interfacial stability. These findings collectively advance the development of high-efficiency, scalable tandem photovoltaics for commercialization.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Ga-gradient bandgap engineering improves CIGS bandgap matching in tandem cells",
    "Alkali post-deposition treatments reduce interfacial recombination losses",
    "Ag alloying enables low-temperature growth and bifacial operation of CIGS absorbers"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a unified framework for optimizing CIGS bottom cells to enable high-efficiency, industrially viable perovskite/CIGS tandem solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated mitophagy-related molecular markers in atherosclerotic plaques using transcriptomic analysis of carotid tissue. Paired differential expression analysis identified 107 mitophagy-related genes, with machine learning selecting HAND2, NRP1, and RNF213 as consensus markers. External validation confirmed these markers in independent cohorts, and in vivo experiments showed elevated MLXIP protein in atherosclerotic mice. The findings suggest a mitophagy-immune axis in plaque pathogenesis and require further validation.",
  "key_findings": [
    "HAND2, NRP1, and RNF213 were identified as mitophagy-related markers consistently across paired plaque and control samples",
    "External validation confirmed all three markers in an independent cohort with directional reproducibility",
    "In vivo experiments demonstrated 37.7-fold higher MLXIP protein in atherosclerotic mouse models compared to controls"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study provides preliminary evidence for mitophagy-related molecular markers in atherosclerosis, highlighting a potential mitophagy-immune axis that may inform future plaque-targeted therapeutic strategies."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing anti-ambipolar stability in n-type organic mixed-conductors for neuromorphic applications. By blending P(gNDI-gT2) with PMMA, the researchers achieved mechanically stable and ion-permeable frameworks that prevent structural damage during operation. The approach enabled low-power, fast-spiking Hodgkin-Huxley neurons with tunable dynamics, supporting frequency deconvolution and reservoir computing without optimized device geometries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Blending P(gNDI-gT2) with PMMA stabilized anti-ambipolar characteristics in organic mixed-conductors",
    "The polymer blend reduced swelling-induced structural damage, enabling durable device operation",
    "Modulated blend ratios produced tunable, low-power spiking neurons for reservoir computing"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates a material strategy to achieve stable anti-ambipolar behavior in organic mixed-conductors, advancing neuromorphic system design through robust, tunable spiking neuron implementations."
}

{
  "summary": "This review investigates how glutaminase isoform composition (GAC/KGA) and splice-variants in hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) influence redox balance, ferroptosis sensitivity, and therapeutic resistance. It highlights EGFR-AKT-WTAP-mediated splicing favoring GAC, S1.00A14-mediated stabilization contributing to sorafenib resistance, and the indirect NADPH phenotype associated with GAC. The study emphasizes the need for isoform-specific targeting strategies and clinical validation of splice-switching approaches like ASO5.",
  "key_findings": [
    "EGFR-AKT-WTAP-mediated splicing favors GAC isoform expression in HCC",
    "S100A14-mediated GLS/KGA stabilization promotes sorafenib resistance in selected HCC models",
    "GAC-associated NADPH phenotype is indirect, as glutaminase does not directly produce NADPH"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study clarifies the role of glutaminase isoform dynamics in HCC redox regulation, providing a foundation for isoform-targeted therapies to overcome treatment resistance and enhance ferroptosis sensitivity."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates optimizing solar interfacial evaporation efficiency by synergistically managing water state and thermal effects. The researchers engineered a wood-based biomass framework with hydrophilic micron-to-submicron hierarchical pores to balance water transport capacity and activity, inducing loosely bound intermediate water with low vaporization enthalpy. This design enhanced thermal effects to 50.7°C and achieved a record evaporation rate of . The system also exhibited superior salt repellency and antifouling properties, offering a scalable, low-cost solution for freshwater production.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Induced loosely bound intermediate water with low vaporization enthalpy through hydrophilic hierarchical pores",
    "Achieved temperature up to 50.7°C and evaporation rate of 5.12 kg m-2 h-1",
    "Demonstrated salt repellency and antifouling capabilities via hierarchical pore structure and surface polar groups"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a water-heat synergistic strategy for highly efficient solar evaporation, advancing sustainable freshwater production through biomimetic design principles."
}

{
  "summary": "This review investigates mitochondrial metabolic reprogramming in the tumor microenvironment as a mechanism driving immunotherapy resistance. It synthesizes how tumor cell and immune cell metabolic changes promote immunosuppression, leading to antitumor immunity exhaustion. The study identifies key metabolite-mediated pathways that facilitate immune evasion and evaluates strategies targeting mitochondrial metabolism to overcome resistance, highlighting current challenges and future directions in metabolism-focused immunotherapy.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Mitochondrial metabolic reprogramming in tumor cells and immune cells contributes to immunosuppressive tumor microenvironments",
    "Metabolite exchange between tumor cells and immune cells drives antitumor immunity exhaustion",
    "Targeting mitochondrial metabolism offers potential strategies to overcome immunotherapy resistance"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review provides a mechanistic framework for understanding how mitochondrial metabolic reprogramming enables tumor immune evasion and informs the development of metabolism-targeted immunotherapeutic approaches."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the inaccuracy of water vapor transmission rate (WVTR) measurements in gravimetric wet-cup tests by modeling apparatus resistance as a series component. The calibrated model reduces deviations from reference permeability for poly(dimethylsiloxane) membranes and highly permeable anion-exchange membranes, improving accuracy from 49.8% to 6.2% mean absolute relative deviation. It provides a method to convert WVTR to intrinsic water vapor permeability (W. WVP) while accounting for air-gap effects and measurement geometry.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Calibrated model reduces WVTR deviation from reference permeability for poly(dimethylsiloxane) membranes",
    "Model improves accuracy for highly permeable anion-exchange membranes, reducing mean absolute relative deviation from 49.8% to 6.2%",
    "The model provides criteria for geometry selection and measurement duration, enabling conversion of WVTR to intrinsic water vapor permeability (WVP)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a method to accurately convert WVTR measurements to intrinsic water vapor permeability by accounting for apparatus resistance, resolving a critical limitation in assessing membrane breathability for skin-interfaced electronics."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines regulatory T cell (Treg) interactions within the bone marrow microenvironment under homeostasis and disease. It describes how Tregs influence hematopoietic stem cells, mesenchym. stromal cells, and immune cells via direct contact or secreted factors. The study highlights disease-related disruptions in Treg function linked to multiple myeloma, myelodysplastic syndromes, and other hematologic disorders. It also discusses therapeutic strategies targeting Treg modulation to restore immune balance and blood cell production.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Tregs maintain immune balance in bone marrow niches through interactions with surrounding cells",
    "Disease conditions alter Treg numbers and functions, contributing to hematologic disorders",
    "Therapeutic approaches focus on modulating Treg activity to restore homeostasis in blood cell production"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review provides a comprehensive framework for understanding Treg-mediated bone marrow homeostasis and its disruption in hematologic diseases, informing potential therapeutic strategies for immune dysregulation."
}
